cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "softdecode: soft-decision demapping over fading optical channels, including the mismatched-channel-state penalty"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Exact log-likelihood ratios for on-off keying and M-ary pulse-position
  modulation over unit-mean lognormal and gamma-gamma fading under a
  thermal-limited, signal-independent additive Gaussian noise model, with the
  fading average taken by a quadrature rule that is verified against a Monte
  Carlo estimate of the same integral and against the textbook affine
  log-likelihood ratio in the zero-scintillation limit; the measured cost of
  the max-log approximation and of log-likelihood-ratio clipping, reported both
  in log-likelihood-ratio error and in decoded bit error rate because the two
  disagree; the mismatched-channel-state penalty measured separately for
  over-estimated and under-estimated channel quality, which is not symmetric,
  together with the decision-threshold mechanism that makes it asymmetric; and
  a learned log-likelihood-ratio corrector for the mismatched regime,
  benchmarked on a disjoint reporting split against the true-channel-state
  bound, max-log with the estimated channel state, the analytic
  posterior-aware log-likelihood ratio, and tuned scalar rescaling and
  clipping of the plug-in log-likelihood ratio. The analytic posterior-aware
  log-likelihood ratio beats the learned corrector in every regime measured and
  that is published as the result. Validation level 2, research grade. Not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - free-space-optical
  - log-likelihood-ratio
  - soft-decision-demapping
  - lognormal-fading
  - gamma-gamma
  - on-off-keying
  - pulse-position-modulation
  - channel-state-information
  - ldpc
